# tools/ales_loop_witness.rish — the transport loop: a marked region read round and round (ALES14).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES14.
# Design read: active-designing/20260814-fill-ales14-lotus-transport-loop.md
# Stands on: lotus/transport.rye (ALES7) — the play head this rung extends (a loop OFF delegates to it whole); lotus/clock.rye
# (ALES5) — mark_ms sets the region in real time; lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2) — the Clip the master is.
#
# lotus/loop.rye extends ALES7's forward play head with a marked region [start, end) it WRAPS at instead of stopping — the
# first read that does not end. A loop OFF is ALES7 exactly; a loop ON cycles the region forever, the head kept within
# [start,end) so K cycles concatenate to the region repeated K times. The selftest proves: a loop off matches the forward
# read; a region [1,4) cycles 20,30,40,… exactly; the head stays within the region at any block size; a whole-master loop
# replays continuously; a single-sample region repeats; make refuses BadLoop; mark_ms places the region in real time; the loop
# reads only, never mutating the master. Purely local — no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_loop_witness.rish

say "ales-loop: Language EN — ALES14 reads a marked region round and round: the practice loop, the comping cycle — the first read that does not end."
say "ales-loop: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: a loop is a play head that WRAPS at a marked end instead of stopping, the head kept within the region so K cycles concatenate to the region repeated K times, no seam sample skipped or doubled."
say "ales-loop: Lens TAME — a loop OFF delegates to ALES7's read whole (the loop generalizes the transport); no new arithmetic; make refuses BadLoop by name; region bounds proven within the master; read-only, never mutating the master; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/loop"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/loop.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-loop: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/loop.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-loop: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-loop: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-loop' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-loop: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-loop line"

say "ales-loop: GREEN — the transport loop cycles a marked region exactly, the head kept within it, a loop off reading identically to ALES7. The next Lotus rung can name a stereo transport, a scrub window, or a punch region tying playback back to capture."
